# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# GeometryOptimization LBFGS, CG, and GradientDescent call the spec potential.
# The callback stops at the problem Euclidean force norm, or the noise-aware rule.
# v2 success is under the cap, at that stop, and Hessian index 0.
# Noise is added after the clean call. The index uses the clean Hessian.
# GeometryOptimization 0.1.6 OptimLBFGS uses the Hager-Zhang initial step. BackTracking linesearch of order 2 and maxstep 0.8 bohr. The iteration ceiling is the force-call cap. The potential is the harness callback. Sigma is 0, so the stop is the clean Euclidean force norm 0.01. The index is the clean Hessian with the rigid-mode rule. Positions are labeled bohr and the energy is labeled hartree, so austrip leaves the spec numbers unchanged.
